{#
Generated by: Claude Code CLI
Date time: 2026/09/07 02:40 SAST
Version: 0.6
Description:
  The one distribution chart on the platform: a labelled horizontal bar per row, with its figure.

  Core owns it and there is no charting library anywhere near it. A bar chart is a div with a width,
  and a library would add a network dependency, a script that must run before anything is legible,
  and a canvas that a screen reader cannot read. This renders server-side, needs no JavaScript, and
  the numbers are present as text whether or not the bars draw at all.

  Bars are scaled against the largest row rather than the total, and that share is computed in the
  service. A catalogue spread evenly over sixteen branches would draw sixteen bars at six percent
  each and say nothing; against the largest, the shape is legible whatever the spread. The figure
  beside each bar is the real count, so the scaling never has to be guessed at.

  Included with one array so a screen can show more than one distribution without them sharing state.

  Comments here are plain prose only: no angle brackets, no comment delimiters, no template tokens
  and no code. Each of those is read as markup rather than as text.

Changelog:
  2026/09/07 02:40 SAST
  - Created for the v0.6 taxonomy distribution charts.
#}
<div class="cl-chart" role="table" aria-label="{{ dc_label }}">
	{% for dc_row in dc_rows %}
		<div class="cl-chart-row" role="row">
			<span class="cl-chart-label" role="rowheader">{{ dc_row.label }}</span>
			<span class="cl-chart-track"><span class="cl-chart-bar" style="width:{{ dc_row.share }}%"></span></span>
			<span class="cl-chart-value" role="cell">{{ dc_row.total }}</span>
		</div>
	{% endfor %}
</div>
